  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prevention of Violent Extremism through Social Accountability in Ghana (PoVETSA) Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Prevention of Violent Extremism through Social Accountability (PoVETSA) Project will support national peacebuilding institutions to improve public trust and civilian confidence in security services. The project will embark on trust-building mechanism for Ghanaian national peace building institutions and the community they seek to serve. It will promote accountable and responsive security sector to  counter the push and pull factors of violent extremism and thereby engender an improved relationship between communities and the security services for the prevention of violent extremism. Strategic events such as a National Dialogue bringing together Civilians and security services on improving civilian-security agency relations for the prevention of violent extremism will be held in Accra, the national capital. Technical Committee Meetings will be held to draft national Framework for Improving Civilian-Security agency relations for the prevention of violent extremism. Other regional engagements will be held in Northern Region due to the Region&#x2019;s proximity to Burkina Faso and C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire which have experienced violent extremism recently as well as incidents of civilian-police-military clashes and active ongoing conflicts which many fear could trigger violent extremism. Target beneficiaries include youth groups, top-level hierarchy of the Ghana Police Service, the Ghana armed forces, Ghana Immigration Service, Ministry of National Security, Ministry of Justice, Ministry of Interior, Defense Ministry, CSOs, and other Civilian groups etc.</narrative>
  </description>
